  "body": "## What changed\n\nFollow-up to #690 / #694. Mill generators seed their `PathBuilder` at (0, 0, clearance) and rapid to their start. When the start is exactly X0 Y0, that rapid has zero length and the builder drops it, so the first posted motion was a feed from the tool-change position (#690's bug through another door).\n\n- **`crates/cl/src/cl/path.rs`:** a new `PathBuilder::approached(seed)`. If a path's first move would not be a rapid, the builder states a zero-length rapid at the seed first.\n  - It happens before any move is recorded, so cycle and comp-span indices never shift.\n  - It's opt-in: `new()` is unchanged, so drilling, ladders and the lathe keep their openings byte for byte.\n- **The 19 motion files** that seeded `PathBuilder::new(Point3::new(0.0, 0.0, p.clearance_z))` now use `approached`. Face's #694-only insert is removed in favour of the shared rule.\n- **Decision record:** `docs/decisions/697-approached-builder.md`.\n\n## Pinned by\n\n`crates/motion/tests/origin_approach.rs` (new, 5 tests):\n- `a_start_at_the_seed_still_opens_with_a_rapid`\n- `an_arc_first_move_is_approached_too`\n- `a_path_that_opens_with_its_own_rapid_is_unchanged`\n- `a_plain_builder_keeps_its_old_behaviour`\n- `no_generator_seeds_the_clearance_plane_without_the_approach_law` (a source scan, so a new generator can't reintroduce it)\n\n`machining2d::a_face_entering_at_the_origin_still_opens_with_its_approach` from #694 still passes through the shared rule.\n\n## How tested\n\nOn upstream main 4aec95a9 plus this commit:\n- **cl and motion:** every `camcraft-cl` and `camcraft-motion` suite passes, and clippy on both with `--tests` is clean.\n- **app:** every `camcraft-app` suite and `--lib` pass, apart from two known breaks on main:\n  - `lathe_thread_travel` doesn't build (#686).\n  - `probe_dialects` fails 3/13 on main; #700 fixes it.\n- **Goldens:** no app golden changed, so no existing fixture starts exactly at X0 Y0. Every existing program is byte-identical.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThe lathe generators (blade, parting, contour door and rides) seed at a clearance radius and station and have their own approach rules, so they're out of scope; noted on the issue. No machine run. The fork is synced at v0.16.0.\n\nChangelog: Mill operations whose start point is exactly X0 Y0 now open with a rapid on the clearance plane instead of a feed from the tool-change position (#697)\n\nFixes #697\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
